"""Build one offline HTML handoff with embedded storyboard, reference and prompts."""
from pathlib import Path
import json, base64, html

root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
out=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
def data(path,mime):return 'data:'+mime+';base64,'+base64.b64encode(path.read_bytes()).decode('ascii')
def esc(value):return html.escape(str(value),quote=True)

prefix='Photorealistic architectural cinema. One consistent white precast commercial entrance with square columns, slim graphite aluminum frames, clear glass, long stainless vertical pull handles, pale terrazzo and California trees. Warm daylight, cool steel-blue reflections, neutral whites. Natural optics, stable straight verticals, plausible hardware, crisp architectural detail. Restrained camera motion. No people, text, logos, floating glass, extra doors, warped mullions, flicker or fantasy construction.'
shots=[
('01','The line','00:00–00:02','0–47','Extreme macro / 100mm feel','A narrow reflection exposes the polished glass edge against a graphite field.','Move slowly left to right along the edge; a small natural highlight travels upward. The glass stays fixed.','End with a pale-blue reflection filling the right side; match its direction into shot 02.','An extreme macro view along the polished edge of a stationary glass lite beside a graphite mullion. One thin white reflected line on a deep graphite background; faint steel-blue reflections. Same material world as the supplied entrance reference. Shallow but usable focus, no glowing neon.','Slow controlled lateral camera move along the stationary glass edge. A real reflected highlight moves gently across the polished edge as the camera changes angle. Keep the edge rigid and straight. End with a pale-blue reflection occupying the right side. No object deformation.'),
('02','Follow the reflection','00:02–00:04','48–95','Close oblique / 65mm feel','Sky and trees travel across the glass as parallax reveals a mullion.','Continue left-to-right camera travel; hold the actual glass plane still.','A dark vertical mullion crosses the center at the cut; match to the framing joint.','Very close oblique view of the reference entrance glass. Blue sky and one tree reflected in a stationary clear pane; graphite mullion at right, narrow warm sunlight reflection. Keep reflections optically plausible.','Track slowly left to right parallel to the glass facade. Reflected trees shift naturally through camera parallax while the aluminum stays fixed. Let a dark vertical mullion move through the center near the end. No independent sliding reflections or rippling glass.'),
('03','The joint','00:04–00:06','96–143','Macro / 85mm feel','A small framing joint becomes a strong geometric composition.','Slide down the mullion a few inches with a gentle focus change to the gasket.','Match the lower horizontal member to the threshold line in shot 04.','Macro architectural photograph of the junction between one horizontal and one vertical graphite aluminum member at the same entrance. Real black gasket, subtle machining texture, flush alignment. Straight square members; no decorative bolts.','A restrained downward slider move along the rigid mullion, ending on the horizontal joint. A very subtle focus change resolves the gasket edge. Keep the frame geometry completely stable; no parts grow, move or assemble.'),
('04','Light on the threshold','00:06–00:08','144–191','Floor-height macro / 65mm feel','A hard stripe of sunlight cuts across the threshold and terrazzo.','Track forward a few inches toward the base of the door.','Carry the diagonal sunlight stripe into the wider doorway composition.','Low macro view of the fixed bottom threshold and seal at the reference graphite glass entrance. Pale terrazzo with fine aggregate. One sharp diagonal band of real sunlight. No debris, hands or tools.','Slow floor-level push toward the fixed threshold. Preserve exact floor joints, threshold profile and straight frame. The sunlight remains stable. Only subtle real parallax; no liquid floor reflections or animated sealant.'),
('05','The opening','00:08–00:10','192–239','Three-quarter entrance / 35mm feel','The right-hand entrance door opens on its normal hinge.','Camera eases forward as a single door leaf moves outward through a small believable arc.','Cut while the right-hand jamb travels past the camera edge.','Three-quarter view of the same white commercial entrance, with one graphite glass door nearly closed and its stainless vertical pull clearly visible. Warm lobby beyond. Reference columns, frame divisions and handles must match. No person.','The single right-hand glass door swings slowly outward on its existing hinges, as if opened from outside the frame. A restrained camera push approaches the opening. Preserve the hinge side, handle and all mullions. The door is rigid; it does not slide, dissolve, duplicate or bend. If door motion fails, keep it open and animate only the camera.'),
('06','Cross the threshold','00:10–00:12','240–287','Low forward dolly / 28mm feel','The camera passes through the already-open doorway into the lobby.','Smooth low dolly inward; a real jamb briefly masks the side of frame.','Use the jamb as a practical wipe into the broader interior.','Low camera just outside the already-open reference entrance, looking inward through the central clear opening. Square white columns, warm linear ceiling lights, pale terrazzo joints leading inside. Same door safely outside the camera path.','A smooth stabilized low dolly passes through the existing open doorway into the lobby. The fixed jamb moves naturally past the side of frame. Camera follows an unobstructed path through the opening, never through the glass. Straight columns remain straight; no room stretching.'),
('07','The space beyond','00:12–00:14','288–335','Interior reveal / 28mm feel','The lobby opens into glass office fronts and a clean patch of daylight.','Ease into a calm, level interior view; movement slows.','Intentional cut from afternoon interior to blue-hour exterior; do not morph the building.','A wide restrained view inside the same commercial lobby. White square columns, graphite glass office fronts to the right, warm linear ceiling lights, pale terrazzo. A distinct shaft of late-afternoon sunlight across the floor. No furnishings added.','A very slow level dolly settles into the interior composition. Keep the office-front grid, floor joints and column spacing consistent. Reflections move only from camera motion. End nearly still with clear sightlines and no people.'),
('08','Open for business','00:14–00:16','336–383','Exterior reveal / 35mm feel','A quiet wide shot holds the completed entrance at blue hour.','Small, slow pullback; warm interior lights stay steady.','Hero poster: use a clean frame here. For a loop, finish behind a dark foreground mullion and match-cut to shot 01; otherwise use an intentional cut.','Wide three-quarter exterior view of the SAME white precast commercial entrance at blue hour. Same square columns, graphite door frames and stainless pulls, warm interior light through clear glass, pale steel-blue sky, California planting. No signs or people.','A slow restrained pullback from the completed glass entrance at blue hour. Warm interior light is steady and the building stays rigid. A fixed foreground mullion can cover one edge toward the finish for a practical edit into the macro opening. No accelerated timelapse, magical light switches or extra architecture.')
]
manifest={'title':'THE THRESHOLD','version':1,'created':'2026-10-31','status':'Storyboard and production plan; generated video not included','duration_seconds':16,'fps':24,'edited_frames':384,'reference':'Embedded entrance-reference image is the continuity anchor. Storyboard is visual direction, not a clean model input.','master_style':prefix,'negative_prompt':'flicker, breathing architecture, bent mullions, duplicated handles, floating glass, drifting geometry, melted metal, ghosting, jitter, impossible reflections, people, faces, text, invented logo, signage, neon holograms, extreme lens distortion','storyboard_generation_prompt':(out/'STORYBOARD-PROMPT.txt').read_text(encoding='utf-8'),'shots':[]}
cards=''
for number,title,time,frames,lens,beat,camera,transition,still,motion in shots:
    full_still=prefix+' '+still
    full_motion=prefix+' '+motion
    manifest['shots'].append({'id':number,'title':title,'timecode':time,'frame_range_24fps':frames,'edit_seconds':2,'lens_intent':lens,'beat':beat,'camera':camera,'transition':transition,'clean_keyframe_prompt':full_still,'image_to_video_prompt':full_motion,'source_generation':'Generate about 4 seconds if supported; choose the strongest stable 48-frame segment. Use the nearest native supported duration/frame count, then trim in the edit.'})
    cards+=f'''<article id="shot-{number}"><div class="shot-top"><span>{number} / {esc(time)}</span><span>48 EDIT FRAMES</span></div><h3>{esc(title)}</h3><p>{esc(beat)}</p><dl><dt>Camera</dt><dd>{esc(camera)}</dd><dt>Lens intent</dt><dd>{esc(lens)}</dd><dt>Transition</dt><dd>{esc(transition)}</dd></dl><details><summary>Clean keyframe prompt</summary><pre>{esc(full_still)}</pre></details><details open><summary>Image-to-video prompt</summary><pre>{esc(full_motion)}</pre></details></article>'''

board=data(out/'storyboard.png','image/png')
reference=data(root/'creative/video-concepts-2026-10-31/entrance-light.png','image/png')
logo=data(root/'site/assets/logo.svg','image/svg+xml')
handoff='''Rebuff: Produce the CGC hero film THE THRESHOLD using the user's local video-generation models. This HTML is the complete handoff; all media, prompts and instructions are embedded. Do not depend on the original repository paths to read this file.

1. Read the master direction and all eight shot cards. Extract the embedded entrance reference and storyboard with the download links. The board is a visual guide, not a single video input. Generate a clean, unnumbered still for each shot from its keyframe prompt and the common entrance reference. Inspect and correct continuity before video generation.
2. Use image-to-video with those accepted keyframes, one shot at a time. Do not animate the entire board. Use the installed model's native frame count/resolution; no invented ComfyUI node IDs or assumed model settings. Generate roughly four seconds per shot when supported and keep the best two seconds. Save the actual workflow/model/settings/seed alongside each result for repeatability. A shared seed alone does not guarantee continuity.
3. Assemble eight two-second shots at 24fps, total 384 frames / 16 seconds. Use the listed practical match cuts. Do not dissolve between different building geometries. Check every frame for frame/handle deformation, reflection instability and camera paths through glass. Replace failed door motion with a camera-only shot of an already-open door.
4. Deliver a silent desktop hero MP4 and WebM, a separately composed phone version, a clean poster for each, captions describing visible scenes and an edit manifest with provenance. Match the current site's asset contract below. Generated footage must be visibly disclosed as an architectural concept, never a real CGC job.
5. If repository access is available, read cgc/STATUS.md and the current cgc/_work/architectural.py before editing. Preserve the chosen bright palette, exact consent copy, facts, accessibility and API schema. Replace the concept poster/manual field-film arrangement only after the generated video passes visual review. Never autoplay with reduced motion; preserve pause/play, CC, hidden-tab/out-of-view pause and poster-first behavior.
6. Run the relevant browser checks at 360/390/430/1440 and reduced motion. Commit small changes on the current branch. Do not push, change DNS or Deployment Protection, create credentials, or promote production. Report failures and missing dependencies honestly. Do not send messages or publish elsewhere.'''

page=f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>CGC / The Threshold — local video production handoff</title><style>
:root{{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#172126;background:#fff;line-height:1.6}}*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0}}header{{padding:24px 5%;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd3d8;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;align-items:center}}header img{{width:140px;height:auto}}header p,.label{{font:11px/1.7 monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}}main{{max-width:1280px;margin:auto;padding:48px 32px}}h1{{font-size:clamp(48px,9vw,114px);letter-spacing:-.06em;line-height:.95;margin:20px 0 28px}}h2{{font-size:34px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:0 0 24px}}h3{{font-size:28px;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.1;margin:20px 0 14px}}p{{margin:0 0 20px;max-width:800px}}section{{padding:40px 0;border-top:1px solid #cbd3d8;margin-top:40px}}.intro{{font-size:21px;max-width:780px}}.actions{{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin:24px 0}}a.button,button{{min-height:48px;min-width:44px;padding:12px 18px;border:1px solid #39586c;border-radius:4px;background:#39586c;color:white;text-decoration:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:14px;cursor:pointer}}a.button.secondary{{background:white;color:#172126;border-color:#cbd3d8}}:focus-visible{{outline:3px solid #39586c;outline-offset:4px}}img{{max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block}}.board{{max-width:880px;margin:auto}}figcaption{{font-size:12px;color:#526169;margin-top:16px}}figure{{margin:0}}.specs{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:0;border:1px solid #cbd3d8;margin:32px 0}}.specs div{{padding:18px;border-right:1px solid #cbd3d8}}.specs div:last-child{{border:0}}.specs b{{display:block;font-size:24px}}.specs span{{font-size:12px;color:#526169}}.shots{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:32px}}article{{padding:24px;border:1px solid #cbd3d8;min-width:0}}.shot-top{{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;font:11px/1.6 monospace;color:#526169}}dl{{font-size:13px}}dt{{font-weight:bold;margin-top:14px}}dd{{margin:4px 0 18px;color:#526169}}details{{border-top:1px solid #cbd3d8;padding:12px 0}}summary{{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;display:list-item;padding:8px 0;font-size:13px}}pre{{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.7 monospace;padding:18px;background:#edf1f3;margin:12px 0 0}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px}}td,th{{border-bottom:1px solid #cbd3d8;text-align:left;padding:12px;vertical-align:top}}code{{overflow-wrap:anywhere}}.note{{padding:22px;border-left:3px solid #39586c;background:#edf1f3}}li{{margin-bottom:12px}}footer{{padding:30px 32px;border-top:1px solid #cbd3d8;font-size:12px;color:#526169}}#copy-status{{font-size:13px;min-height:24px}}@media(max-width:700px){{main{{padding:32px 20px}}header{{padding:20px}}header p{{font-size:9px}}.shots{{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.specs{{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}.specs div{{border-bottom:1px solid #cbd3d8}}article{{padding:20px}}table{{font-size:11px}}td,th{{padding:10px 6px}}}}@media print{{header,button,.actions{{display:none}}main{{max-width:none;padding:0}}details:not([open])>pre{{display:block}}.shots{{display:block}}article{{break-inside:avoid;margin:16px 0}}section{{break-before:auto}}}}
</style></head><body><header><img src="{logo}" alt="Commercial Glazing Contractors Inc."><p>Local video production handoff<br>October 31, 2026 / version 1</p></header><main><span class="label">One file / all reference media and prompts embedded / works offline</span><h1>THE<br>THRESHOLD.</h1><p class="intro">A line of light becomes a glass edge. Reflections lead us to the frame. An opening becomes a place.</p><p>Eight connected architectural shots, built for separate local generation and a disciplined 16-second edit. The contrast comes from intimate material detail and a wide spatial reveal.</p><div class="specs"><div><b>16 sec</b><span>Final edit</span></div><div><b>8 shots</b><span>2 seconds each</span></div><div><b>24 fps</b><span>384 edited frames</span></div><div><b>16:9 + 9:16</b><span>Separate framing</span></div></div><p class="note"><strong>This is a generated storyboard and production plan.</strong> It does not contain completed generated video or depict a verified CGC project. The images are architectural concepts. This file makes no network requests.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#handoff">Instructions for Rebuff</a><a class="button secondary" href="#shots">Eight shot prompts</a><button id="save-json">Save production JSON</button></div><section id="board"><span class="label">Visual sequence / read left to right, top to bottom</span><h2>From an edge to an entrance.</h2><figure class="board"><img id="board-image" src="{board}" alt="Eight-frame generated storyboard: glass edge, reflection, framing joint, threshold, opening door, passage, interior and blue-hour entrance" width="1024" height="1536"><figcaption>Storyboard generated with the built-in image generator using the entrance reference below. Frame numbers belong to the board only; generate clean keyframes without numbers or borders.</figcaption></figure><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="{board}" download="CGC-The-Threshold-storyboard.png">Save storyboard PNG</a></div></section><section id="reference"><h2>One building. One material language.</h2><figure><img id="entrance-reference" src="{reference}" alt="Generated reference of the graphite-framed glass entrance, white columns and pale terrazzo lobby" width="1672" height="941"><figcaption>Use this image as the continuity anchor. Preserve column positions, mullion divisions, door hinge side, pull handles and floor material. Shot 08 changes the time of day intentionally.</figcaption></figure><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="{reference}" download="CGC-entrance-reference.png">Save entrance reference</a><a class="button secondary" href="{logo}" download="CGC-supplied-logo.svg">Save supplied logo</a></div><h3>Master direction</h3><pre>{esc(prefix)}</pre><h3>Negative prompt / rejection criteria</h3><pre>{esc(manifest['negative_prompt'])}</pre></section><section id="shots"><span class="label">Generate independently / assemble in the edit</span><h2>Eight shots. One movement.</h2><p>Generate clean stills first, using the same entrance reference. Then animate those accepted stills. Where supported, produce around four seconds per shot and choose the best stable two seconds. Adapt frame counts to your installed model; the final edit is 24fps. Lens values describe the look, not required model parameters.</p><div class="shots">{cards}</div></section><section id="workflow"><h2>Local production order.</h2><ol><li>Choose the installed image/video models and verify available VRAM, native resolution and duration. This pack is model-agnostic; it does not claim to include an executable ComfyUI graph.</li><li>Create eight clean keyframes with the reference, master direction and per-shot keyframe prompts. Reject inconsistent mullions, handles or floor joints before generating motion.</li><li>Animate one accepted still at a time with its motion prompt. Avoid generating the entire sequence in one long request. Use reference controls your model supports; record the exact workflow, model, seed and settings.</li><li>Prefer one controlled camera movement per shot. If shot 05's hinge motion fails, use an already-open door and a camera-only move. Do not repeatedly regenerate the whole film for one failed shot.</li><li>Trim each to 48 usable frames at 24fps. If a model outputs another rate, conform and inspect cadence. Do not interpolate unstable glass edges. Use practical match cuts, not building morphs.</li><li>Keep the camera's action near the center for the portrait version, but compose a separate 9:16 pass where the crop loses the doorway. The central 31.6% of a 16:9 image is the same-height 9:16 crop; a 60% safety area does not guarantee portrait framing.</li><li>Use no typography inside generated footage. Keep website text as HTML. Use the supplied SVG only for an optional social-film end card, added in editing.</li><li>Make a silent website master. Optional social sound: a quiet material click at 04s, a subtle threshold step at 08s, a soft spatial tone at 12s. Use original/licensed sound; no scraped music.</li></ol><h3>Loop and fallback</h3><p>The main 16-second version can end on a clean wide hold. For looping, use a real dark mullion wipe or an intentional edit back to the macro edge. Check the join frame by frame; do not claim a perfect loop until the exported clip is reviewed. Pick the strongest clean frame from shot 05 or 08 as the poster. Reduced-motion visitors see that poster without autoplay.</p></section><section id="delivery"><h2>Website delivery contract.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Target</th><th>Requirements</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>hero-desktop.mp4 / .webm</code></td><td>1600×900, 16s, 24fps</td><td>Silent, MP4 H.264 yuv420p + faststart, WebM VP9; aim ≤4MB each. Inspect glass edges after encoding.</td></tr><tr><td><code>hero-mobile.mp4 / .webm</code></td><td>720×1280, 16s, 24fps</td><td>Dedicated portrait composition; preserve the doorway. Aim ≤3MB each.</td></tr><tr><td><code>hero-desktop-poster.webp</code></td><td>1600×900</td><td>Clean stable frame, no baked text; responsive smaller variant.</td></tr><tr><td><code>hero-mobile-poster.webp</code></td><td>720×1280</td><td>Match the portrait clip; no motion blur.</td></tr><tr><td><code>hero-captions.vtt</code></td><td>UTF-8 WebVTT</td><td>Describe what the accepted edit actually shows; draft below.</td></tr><tr><td><code>edit.json</code></td><td>Shot provenance</td><td>Actual model/workflow/seed/source outputs, trims, rates, dates and concept disclosure; never save credentials.</td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Draft captions — revise to match the accepted edit</summary><pre>WEBVTT

00:00.000 --&gt; 00:04.000
Light traces a glass edge; reflected sky moves across the pane.

00:04.000 --&gt; 00:08.000
Close views of graphite framing and a sunlit entrance threshold.

00:08.000 --&gt; 00:12.000
A glass door opens; the camera moves through the doorway.

00:12.000 --&gt; 00:16.000
Glass office fronts inside, then a warm entrance at blue hour.
</pre></details><p>Integration checks: visible generated-concept disclosure; pause/play and CC; stop when hidden or off-screen; no automatic loading with reduced motion; no scroll trap; 44px controls; 16px inputs; 360/390/430/1440 layouts; no console errors or horizontal overflow; preserve bid form and CRM.</p></section><section id="handoff"><h2>Give this file to Rebuff.</h2><p>Send this HTML itself. It contains everything shown above, including the full-size board, reference and logo. No separate attachment folder is required.</p><button id="copy-handoff">Copy Rebuff instructions</button><p id="copy-status" role="status"></p><pre id="handoff-text">{esc(handoff)}</pre></section></main><footer>Commercial Glazing Contractors Inc. / C-17 · LIC 1109661. Storyboard is an illustrative concept. No client work, reviews or project statistics are invented.</footer><script type="application/json" id="production-manifest">{json.dumps(manifest).replace('<','\\u003c')}</script><script>
document.getElementById('save-json').onclick=()=>{{const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([document.getElementById('production-manifest').textContent],{{type:'application/json'}}));a.download='CGC-The-Threshold-production.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000)}};
document.getElementById('copy-handoff').onclick=async()=>{{const text=document.getElementById('handoff-text').textContent;try{{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);document.getElementById('copy-status').textContent='Copied.'}}catch{{const range=document.createRange();range.selectNodeContents(document.getElementById('handoff-text'));const selection=window.getSelection();selection.removeAllRanges();selection.addRange(range);document.getElementById('copy-status').textContent='Instructions selected. Use Copy.'}}}};
</script></body></html>'''
(out/'CGC-The-Threshold-Handoff.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
(out/'production.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Created offline single-file handoff:',(out/'CGC-The-Threshold-Handoff.html').stat().st_size,'bytes')
